From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi_drv_sta_set_flags: create the WDS STA netdev on authorization

Companion to rdk-wifi-libhostap 0003/0004, which stop hostapd creating the 4-address
WDS STA netdev before the 4-way handshake (creating it early diverts the station's
pre-auth EAPOL M4 to the WDS netdev on mac80211_hwsim, so the 4-way times out with
reason 15). Something must still create it once the station authorizes. The
UNEXPECTED_4ADDR event is not a reliable trigger: a WDS netdev left over from an
earlier association -- the hwsim phy outlives an LXD container, so <vap>.sta<aid>
survives a recreate -- makes the kernel deliver the 4-addr frames to that (unenslaved)
netdev instead of raising UNEXPECTED_4ADDR, so the station associates and completes the
4-way but never regains a bridge port. Drive it instead from the SET_STATION(authorized)
path, which the HAL always sees: create the netdev, or re-enslave an existing one
(0015), and leave it forwarding (0014). Gated on a Multi-AP backhaul BSS so ordinary
fronthaul clients are unaffected.
---
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -14787,6 +14787,39 @@
 
     if (!!(total_flags & WPA_STA_AUTHORIZED)) {
         nl80211_read_sta_data(interface, addr);
+#ifdef BANANA_PI_PORT
+        /* meta-cmf-bananapi-vcpe: bring up the 4-address WDS STA netdev now that the station
+         * is AUTHORIZED (the 4-way has completed). Creating it earlier -- at association or on
+         * the first 4-addr frame -- makes mac80211_hwsim divert the station's pre-auth EAPOL
+         * (notably M4) to the WDS netdev before the authenticator receives it, so the 4-way
+         * times out (reason 15); the hostapd side (rdk-wifi-libhostap 0003/0004) therefore
+         * defers WDS-STA setup to authorization. Do it here from the HAL, on the reliably
+         * delivered SET_STATION(authorized) event, because a WDS netdev left over from an
+         * earlier association (e.g. across a OneWifi restart or a container recreate, since
+         * the hwsim phy outlives the container) suppresses the UNEXPECTED_4ADDR event that
+         * would otherwise re-trigger it -- so the station would associate and 4-way but never
+         * get its bridge port back. wifi_drv_set_wds_sta() creates the netdev, or re-enslaves
+         * an existing one (see 0015), and leaves it forwarding (see 0014). Restricted to a
+         * Multi-AP backhaul BSS so ordinary fronthaul clients never get a WDS netdev. */
+        if (interface->vap_info.vap_mode == wifi_vap_mode_ap &&
+            (interface->u.ap.conf.multi_ap & BACKHAUL_BSS)) {
+            struct sta_info *bh_sta = ap_get_sta(&interface->u.ap.hapd, addr);
+
+            if (bh_sta != NULL) {
+                char ifname_wds[IFNAMSIZ + 1] = { 0 };
+
+                interface->u.ap.conf.wds_sta = 1;
+                strncpy(interface->u.ap.conf.wds_bridge, interface->vap_info.bridge_name,
+                    sizeof(interface->u.ap.conf.wds_bridge) - 1);
+                wifi_hal_info_print("%s:%d: STA %s authorized on backhaul %s -- setting up "
+                    "4-address WDS aid=%d bridge=%s\n", __func__, __LINE__,
+                    to_mac_str(addr, mac_str), interface->name, bh_sta->aid,
+                    interface->vap_info.bridge_name);
+                wifi_drv_set_wds_sta(interface, addr, bh_sta->aid, 1,
+                    interface->vap_info.bridge_name, ifname_wds);
+            }
+        }
+#endif // BANANA_PI_PORT
     }
 
     if (!(msg = nl80211_drv_cmd_msg(g_wifi_hal.nl80211_id, interface, 0, NL80211_CMD_SET_STATION)) ||
